{
  "syncVectorsVersion": 1,
  "description": "Cloud Sync end-to-end encryption known answers (WIRE-CONTRACT-V5 section 13.10, section 13.8.1; plans/CC-01-cloud-sync.md section 2.4). A client table, inert to an SDK that has not implemented sync.e2e: a runner reads the named sections it implements. Every row is recomputed by the generator through an independent reference over node:crypto. hkdfCases: HKDF-SHA256 with the exact ikm, salt, info and length, anchored by RFC 5869 appendix A; the label field names the derivation and the info bytes are shown in hex because several labels end in a NUL. envelopeCases: pkey-sync-value/1; a runner opens envelopeHex under rootHex, collection, name and aliases and expects `expect`, and for rows with a `seal` member also seals value with that salt and expects the same bytes (canonical JSON with sorted keys, UTF-8, padded 0x80 then zeros to a multiple of 64, always at least one byte); the invalid reasons are shape, version, kid, auth, padding, json and name, in the order a reader checks them. blindCases: blind(kind, ctx, n). transferPlanCases: the upload mode, partBytes and part count from the stored size and the collection's files.delta. Append-only: a new row or section keeps syncVectorsVersion; a changed row or rule bumps it.",
